WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.837
-Julia and I are about to face
off in a game of "Box of Lies."

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:06.606
All right, here's how it works.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.341
Upstage are nine mystery boxes

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.810
containing objects no one
has ever seen before.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.746
On your turn, you pick up a box,
take out the object,

00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:15.849
and describe it
to your opponent.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:16.883
They have to guess if you're

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.618
lying or telling the truth.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.286
We'll play three rounds.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:23.822
Julia, why don't
you pick the first box.

00:00:23.822 --> 00:00:26.058
-Why, thank you very much.
I shall.

00:00:26.058 --> 00:00:27.794
-You're welcome. Yes.
Oh, 4.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:31.197
-Okay. I don't know.
-The game has already begun.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:34.701
-I'm very excited.
-It looks medium weight.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.203
You didn't struggle, really,
carrying it over,

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.905
so it's not heavy.

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:41.641
All right. Okay.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.047
-Okay.
-Okay.

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.385
-Don't cheat.
-I'm not cheating at all.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.853
I feel like
you're cheating already.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.155
-I'm not cheating.

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:56.989
-Yeah, well, you were,
like, confused at first,

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.558
and then you're amused.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.493
-You're starting to irritate me.
-Really?

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.694
-Yeah.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:04.898
Okay.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:09.668
Okay, so...

00:01:09.668 --> 00:01:12.272
Let me explain something to you.
-Yeah.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:16.543
-You're familiar with something
that's -- A closet, right?

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:17.610
A closet?

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.345
-Yeah. Am I familiar
with a closet?

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.546
Yeah, sure.

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:21.814
I've never heard of that.
What does that word mean?

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:23.249
-Hang on, hang on.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:30.256
And in this closet,
which is miniature, obviously,

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:34.527
there is a horse.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.928
-Okay.

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:42.202
-And it has a huge collection --
Who thinks these up, by the way?

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:44.170
-Well, right now, I think
you're thinking this up.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.072
-You don't know
what I'm about to say.

00:01:47.072 --> 00:01:53.579
A huge collection
of sandals and high heels?

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:57.850
-Okay. Okay.
-And -- Yeah, like, wait.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.419
-Oh, my goodness.
Yeah, 4, 5, 6.

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:01.487
-No, no, no.
I'm looking at the rooms.

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:02.655
-You're counting.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.190
You have the 4, 5, 6,
high heels, and sandals.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.591
Give me a break.

00:02:05.591 --> 00:02:07.393
You're talking about shoes,
because from the interview,

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.661
you were talking about shoes,
and now it's in your head.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.695
-No, I wasn't.

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:11.163
-Yes, you were
talking about high heels

00:02:11.163 --> 00:02:12.298
for the Mark Twain thing.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:15.201
So let me tell you
something -- you lie!

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:19.038
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.340
[ Ding ]

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:24.677
-Oh!

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.012
You know, I've got to
tell you something.

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:28.982
I really pride myself
on being a good liar,

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.284
so I'm incredibly
upset right now.

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:32.452
-Oh, I thought you were
going to say impressed.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:33.452
I thought you were going to
say impressed.

00:02:33.452 --> 00:02:34.487
-No!

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:35.688
-Guys, what number
shall I choose?

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:39.058
[ Indistinct shouting ]
There is no 11.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:41.193
3. Okay.
Somebody yelled "11."

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:43.129
There is no 11.
Thank you, though.

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:46.799
[ Straining ]

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:49.201
-Oh, it must be heavy.

00:02:49.201 --> 00:02:55.208
Wow. That looks so, so heavy.
You poor thing.

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.309
Your arms are killing you.
Yeah.

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:59.378
-My arms are killing me.
Here we go here.

00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:04.350
And that's a...

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.854
Abbondanza.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:08.855
Okay.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:11.223
-Yeah.

00:03:11.223 --> 00:03:13.926
-I feel like I should just
tell you the truth,

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:18.997
because sometimes the truth is
funnier than fiction.

00:03:18.997 --> 00:03:22.968
-Right, but this is called
"Box of Lies," just F.Y.I.

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:25.037
Anyway, carry on.

00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:29.508
-Well, it's two contestants from
"The Masked Singer"

00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:32.979
in a tiny hot tub
filled with Jell-O.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.553
-Two contestants from what?

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:43.389
-"The Masked Singer,"
the show --

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.191
The mystery singers on Fox

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:47.426
with the giant bee heads
and alien heads.

00:03:47.426 --> 00:03:49.662
-First of all, note to self --
I have to watch that show.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:52.899
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
You're missing out.

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:53.966
It's over already.
You missed it.

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:55.501
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.604
-Let me tell you something.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:01.741
I think that you --

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.242
I think you're
telling me the truth.

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:07.046
[ Drumroll ]
Oh, come on.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.082
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.816
-This is the best game
I've ever played.

00:04:10.816 --> 00:04:12.819
Ever!
I've never been this good.

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:13.886
-I hate this game!

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:15.187
-I'm usually terrible
at this game.

00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:16.822
This is great!
-Can I go now?

00:04:16.822 --> 00:04:23.363
-We're doing one more round.
This one is worth 10,000 points.

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:26.965
-Okay, you guys...
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:04:26.965 --> 00:04:28.233
Can -- Wait a minute.

00:04:28.233 --> 00:04:32.337
Can everybody please
just speak once at a time?

00:04:32.337 --> 00:04:33.605
-Yeah.
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:04:33.605 --> 00:04:36.141
-2? 2.
-So, here we go.

00:04:36.141 --> 00:04:37.243
-Okay.
-I'm hot.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.944
-I got to get to 2.
-You can't get me.

00:04:38.944 --> 00:04:41.780
I'm hot, man! I'm hot!

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.983
Ow-wah!
Oh, it's really heavy.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:47.286
Oh, my God. Oh, my goodness.
It's really so heavy.

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.321
Oh, look at how
exhausted you are.

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:51.423
Oh, my God.
-Actually, it's quite light.

00:04:51.423 --> 00:04:52.492
-Oh, it is.
-Okay.

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:54.827
-Oh, it's light? Okay. Wow.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:58.030
Now, I don't know if
that was a lie or true.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:00.533
Okay. Okay.

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.342
How are you? Everything good?

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:13.846
-Are you familiar
with something...

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.615
-This is how you play the game?

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:17.783
Am I familiar with a closet?
Yes.

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:21.320
-Something called a paintbrush?
-Yes, of course.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:22.621
-Okay.

00:05:22.621 --> 00:05:25.391
And...
[ Laughs ]

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:28.961
And have you
ever braided your hair?

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:32.365
Or your wife's hair
or your daughter's hair?

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:33.566
-Yes.

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:39.839
-Okay, so, what this is
a paintbrush of hair

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:44.110
that's been braided with --

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.578
What do you call that thing?

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:48.514
A ponytail holder at the end.

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:51.617
-Like, a scrunchie?
-No, it's not.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:55.087
I said it's a ponytail holder.
Come on. Let's go.

00:05:55.087 --> 00:05:57.423
-What's a ponytail holder?
I've never even heard of that.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:58.524
Why didn't you say,

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.526
"Are you familiar
with ponytail holders?"

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:02.462
I'm not.
-You are not.

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:03.496
-I am not.
I have no idea what that means.

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:04.830
A ponytail holder?

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:07.899
-Well, it's like a thinner thing
that's not a scrunchie.

00:06:07.899 --> 00:06:11.070
-A rubber band?
A rubber band?

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.272
-No, a ponytail holder.

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:16.208
A rubber band is made of rubber
and can tear your hair.

00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:18.544
This is a ponytail holder.
-Made of fabric.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:22.548
-It's also --
There's paint on it and also...

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:26.219
[ Laughter ]
I love this game.

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:27.553
Can I come back
and play again tomorrow?

00:06:27.553 --> 00:06:32.258
-This is unbelievable.
Okay. Gosh.

00:06:32.258 --> 00:06:36.529
-By all means, take your time.

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:40.633
-I'm going to say...you lie.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:42.001
-Whoo!
-Oh, it worked!

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:43.870
[ Dinging ]

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:47.807
Oh, come on!

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:50.075
I was like,
"That's too descriptive.

00:06:50.075 --> 00:06:51.310
That's too good."

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:53.913
Julia Louis-Dreyfus, everybody,
the champion!

